{
  "$comment": [
      "Shared query-semantics cases for SPEC 5.2, the source of truth for every Backyard",
      "document store: the Go backends (internal/docstore/conformance), the Cloudflare",
      "SiteDO and the black-box conformance/ suite. Create each collection's documents in",
      "the listed order (with the given ids, data as the write body), then run each case's",
      "query (the wire Query of POST /db/{c}/query) and expect exactly 'want' (ids, in",
      "order) and 'has_more'. Documents created one after another get strictly increasing",
      "_meta.created_at, and all of them have _meta.version 1. Strings compare by UTF-8",
      "bytes (not UTF-16 code units); every operator only matches values of the same JSON",
      "type, including != and not-in (so '!= null' matches nothing). Numbers compare as",
      "IEEE 754 doubles, as JSON parsers read them (collection 'big': 1760000000123456789",
      "equals 1760000000123456768); keys such as __proto__ or constructor are plain data",
      "fields (collection 'protos': parse the file with JSON.parse, not as a JS literal)."
  ],
